                        "title": "Settlement in Indeterminate Structures",
                        "content": "In statically indeterminate structures, a settlement at a support relieves the constraint at that support. The reaction at B decreases as the support drops, because the beam can now flex more freely. This effect does NOT occur in determinate structures."
