                        "title": "Sway vs. Non-Sway Frame",
                        "content": "In a braced frame, lateral movement is prevented, providing greater restraint (K ≤ 1.0). In an unbraced (sway) frame, joints can translate, reducing effective restraint and increasing effective length (K ≥ 1.0), which reduces the buckling load."
